  # ---- Owned accumulators (spec/alchem-memory.md, "Owned values") ----
  #
  # A fold that puts into its map, and a loop that appends to its string,
  # change the value where it is instead of copying it every turn. The
  # collector's code keeps which values may be changed (a bit per value,
  # gm_map_oput and gm_str_append in spec/memory-x86_64.s); here is how the
  # compiler finds where no program can tell the difference. Three records
  # with no name say it in an environment, each a tag and a position:
  #   53  the name that starts here is the accumulator of a fold: the second
